  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on computing an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes and then favoring the lottery with the higher chance of exceeding this level. The relevant information—such as calculating the mean outcome and assessing which outcomes are above or below it—is not mentioned or implied in the verbal report. Instead, the individual focuses on the certainty of Lottery B and whether the extra 1000 Euros in Lottery A justifies the 20% risk of zero. There is no indication that the individual computed or used any form of aspiration level or evaluated outcomes based on their deviation from such a benchmark. The justification is based on risk aversion and perceived insufficient reward for risk, not on frequency of positive deviations from a reference point. Therefore, while both the reason and the individual favor Lottery B, the underlying logic differs. The match in choice outcome does not imply use of the same reason. The information and rule of the decision reason are not reflected in the individual's deliberation.",
